 "notes": "3 sheets (views 1-3 of the same model), all checked. Notes 1-3 (blue, top-left of sheet 1) are text; the black explanatory paragraphs ('These notes shall be placed on a static annotation plane...', 'Optional: This perpendicularity tolerance is included to legitimize specifying datum target K1.', the long 'Optional: The geometric tolerances applied to datum features D, E, F, G, H, and J...' paragraph on sheet 3) are test-case commentary: not recorded, so notes is not complete. Title: no conventional title block; 'Test Model 2' / 'PMI Complex Test Case 2 - View n (of 3)' are captions (no part name / sheet recorded). GD&T is NOT complete: datum TARGETS are drawn (sheet 1: A1, A2, A3, B1, B2, B3, B4, C1; sheet 2 the same targets plus K1 with target area Ø85) and are not recorded as gdt.datum; datum letters A, B, C, K therefore appear only as targets / in frames. Datum feature symbols recorded: D, E, F, G, H, J (sheet 3). Modifiers: 'MMC'/'LMC' = circled M / circled L on the TOLERANCE value only; datum-reference modifiers are not encoded (sheet 3 profile 0.8 frames are G H(L) J(L), G H J(L), G H(L) J, G H J; profile 0.5 frames are D E(M) F(M), D E(M) F, D E F(M), D E F). Sheet 2 profile frames carry the unequally-disposed modifier: '2.5 (U) 0.5 A B C', '2.5 (U) 2.5 A B C', '2.5 (U) 0 A B C' (U not encoded). Sheet 3 'profile 0.1' applies to datum G, '4 COPLANAR SURFACES'; flatness 0.05 is on datum feature D. Sheet 1 profile 0.25 A B C uses the open arc (profile of a line). Dimensions: only the toleranced sizes printed; note 1 makes all model dimensions basic (none printed). The Ø85 inside the K1 datum-target symbol (target area size) is not recorded as a dimension. Naming rule used for Ø callouts: a callout with an 'nX' count, THRU / depth, or an uppercase (hole) fit is recorded as hole.diameter {diameter, count, upper, lower}; any other Ø size is a dimension {type:'diameter'}. Tolerances are recorded as signed deviations upper/lower; limit dimensions as max/min. GD&T: characteristic in words, datums = the datum letters in order (datum-reference modifiers not encoded), modifiers 'MMC' / 'LMC' = circled M / L after the tolerance value, diameterZone true only where Ø precedes the tolerance."
